{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774388129,"nonce":"nZJ6y3suWCkxLRuF4IQ6m4uMuWA=","title":"Auto-associate session ID with git-bug issues via mandible issue new","message":"Session: 31fa1977-6a49-45f4-af6d-5541a7aed058\n\n## Summary\n\nWhen agents create git-bug issues, there is no automatic association between the issue and the Claude Code session that created it. The session ID (`$MANDIBLE_SESSION_ID`) is available as an env var but is not included in issues by default.\n\n## Why It Matters\n\n- When reviewing bugs later, you want to trace back to the originating conversation context\n- `agent-commit` already links sessions to issues via the Mandible API, but `git-bug bug new` / `mandible issue new` do not\n- Future SDK agents managed by Mandible will have session IDs naturally built into issue creation, but current Claude Code sessions require manual inclusion\n\n## Investigation Points\n\n1. Is `$MANDIBLE_SESSION_ID` reliably available in all agent contexts (main session, subagents, background tasks)?\n2. Does `mandible issue new` already have a `--session` flag or similar? (Checked `mandible issue --help`: no `--session` flag exists as of this filing.)\n3. Could `mandible issue new` automatically include the session ID from the env var when present?\n\n## Proposed Direction\n\n`mandible issue new` should automatically include `Session: \u003cid\u003e` metadata (e.g., as a line in the issue body or as a structured field) when `$MANDIBLE_SESSION_ID` is set in the environment. This would be trivial to implement. For the SDK future, session association would be built into the issue creation API directly.\n\nThis mirrors how `agent-commit --issue \u003cid\u003e` links sessions to issues, but applies to issue creation rather than commit creation.","files":null}]}